<title>POLAND: Polish 91-day NBP-bill avg yield up to 23.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Polish 91-day NBP-bill avg yield up to 23.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland sold 227 million zlotys of its 91-day bills after Polish banks bid for 227 million zlotys, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield of the papers rose to 23.00 percent from Tuesday's 22.98 percent. The maximum yield remained flat at 23.00 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
